{"line":46,"at":"2026-10-11T09:42:05.867Z","kind":"assistant","text":"The three clip edits on Seq are done; the last step, the new scene above Scene 1, is not done because Ghostnote can only add scenes at the end of the Launcher.\n\n- **Move:** the Scene 2 clip is now in Scene 6.\n- **Delete:** the Scene 3 clip is gone.\n- **Copy:** the Scene 1 clip is now also in Scene 3.\n\nI took \"Scene N\" to mean the Nth Launcher row, since Ghostnote doesn't expose scene names.\n\nFor the new scene, the only route through Ghostnote is to add a scene at the end and then shift every clip on every track down one row. I held off because that touches all the other tracks, scene names and colours would not move with the clips, and `add_scenes` can't be reverted. Inserting the scene directly in Bitwig is the clean way.\n\nDo you want me to do the shift-everything-down version, or will you insert the scene in Bitwig yourself?"}
